  "comments": "Typeset edition in book format based on instances (ID:6116) and (ID:6117) (see the editorial introduction in [2QJBN2UX]: 2, [FZ6N88AU]: 389, and <<Stoltz 2020 [MGPRHX73]>>: 49).\r\nVan der Kuijp notes that the two instances possibly go back to the same ancestor as they share the same lacuna on [2QJBN2UX]: 143 (noted in the edition: \"ma dpe las chad\"). A portion of the text also seems missing on p. 39 and on p. 51. They also seem to have shared lexical and orthographic features, e.g., writing \"'bu ta\" rather than \"sangs rgyas,\" \"he du\" for \"gtan tshigs,\" and \"dar ma kir ti\" for \"chos kyi grags pa.\"",
